course: dictionary
lesson: 9817
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word sweating has more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one. Usually it means your body gives out salty drops through your skin. «Heat exhaustion signs include headache, dizziness, feeling sick, being very thirsty, heavy sweating, pale clammy skin and cramps.» Here heavy sweating is a sign that the body is too hot.
explain: Ask yourself what is happening in the sentence. Is it about the body, a feeling, or hard work? Sweating can also mean worrying a lot, as in "I'm sweating about the test." It can also mean working very hard. Pick the meaning that fits the sentence.
explain: Sweat is the salty liquid that comes out of tiny holes in your skin. It helps cool you down when you are hot or exercising. When you are ill, you may sweat a lot too.
fact: Sweating means giving out a salty liquid called sweat through tiny holes in the skin.
fact: You sweat more when you are hot, exercising, ill or nervous.
fact: As sweat dries off the skin, it takes heat away, which cools your body down.
fact: Sweat itself does not smell; bacteria on the skin cause body odour, so wash after sport.
fact: Useful phrases: "sweating buckets" means sweating a lot; "no sweat" means no problem; "cold sweat" means fear.
exercise: «Heat exhaustion signs include headache, dizziness, feeling sick, being very thirsty, heavy sweating, pale clammy skin and cramps.» In this sentence, sweating is a sign that someone is | Winning a race | Bored in class | *Too hot and in trouble with their health | Very clean
exercise: Mia says, «I'm sweating about my spelling test tomorrow.» What does sweating mean here? | *Worrying a lot | Working very hard on a farm | Dripping with water from a glass | Giving out sweat in a hot room
exercise: Dad says, «Don't worry, it's no sweat!» What does no sweat mean? | It is going to rain | *No problem | You must run faster | Nobody is hot
test: «The glass of lemonade on the table was sweating in the sunshine.» What does sweating mean here? | Giving out sweat from the skin | Feeling very worried | *Having tiny drops of water on the outside | Running a race
test: «Jo felt a cold sweat when the teacher called her name.» What does cold sweat suggest? | Feeling very hungry | *Fear or nerves | Winning a prize | A cold day outside
exam: «After the long walk, Ben was sweating buckets, so he drank a big glass of water.» What does sweating buckets mean? | Working in a shop | *Sweating a lot | Feeling very cold | Filling buckets with water
